    <p class="kicker">What has and has not been earned</p>
    <h2 id="t-claim-ledger">The Decimal-Splice Ledger</h2>
    <dl class="evidence-list">
      <dt>Established mathematics <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></dt>
      <dd>Affine normalisation sends \([0,10]\) to \([0,1]\). The half-wave has wavenumber
        \(\pi/10\), midpoint five and endpoint phase \(\pi\). Reflection around five conjugates the centred
        phases. The operator \(-1\) squares to \(+1\).</dd>

      <dt>Selected by the framework <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></dt>
      <dd>The decimal densities are nested from zero; a splice acts on the returning orientation by
        \(S=-1\); and the decimal phase and Prime Plane phase are two descriptions of one clock.</dd>

      <dt>Conditionally sharpened <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></dt>
      <dd>Under those selections, one splice reverses sign, two passages restore it, five is the quadrature
        hinge, and the five-to-four clock is preferred over five-to-eight. The same angle also yields the exact
        weighted-reflection coefficient \(c=1/\varphi\), with strict seam-defect contraction for two
        hypothetical descendants.</dd>

      <dt>Not established</dt>
      <dd>No Hilbert space, field, Hamiltonian, stress–energy tensor or laboratory observable has yet been
        derived. The relation does not establish quantum entanglement, electromagnetism, a new force, a value
        of a dimensional constant or a mechanism for matter–antimatter separation.</dd>

      <dt>Riemann boundary</dt>
      <dd>The Fisher-natural gradient supplies a golden support flow with a unique critical invariant. But
        stationarity of the completed \(\xi\) ledger is exactly RH: every off-line quartet has nonzero divisor
        and residue variation. No principal-prime conservation law proves that stationarity, so the decimal
        splice does not prove RH.</dd>
